          "type": "intro",
          "title": "Indiana Jones Would Be Fired Today",
          "content": "Picture Indiana Jones smashing his way into a tomb, snatching a golden idol, and running off. That's not archaeology — that's **looting**. Modern archaeology is the scientific study of past human societies through their **material remains**: bones, ceramics, soil layers, pollen, isotopes.\n\nThe profession only exists because we stopped digging for treasure and started digging for **information**. Every shard of pottery in context tells us more than a gold mask ripped from its surroundings ever could.\n\nIn this lesson, you'll learn how archaeology evolved from aristocratic curiosity-hunting into a rigorous science — and why the **theoretical debates** between processual and post-processual archaeology still shape every dig today.",
