          "explanation": "The conservation ethic is fundamental: **excavation is destructive and irreversible**. Sealed contexts dug today are gone forever. Future archaeologists will have **DNA from soil, residue chemistry, AI-assisted artifact analysis** we can barely imagine — but only if we leave material in the ground for them. Most modern projects deliberately reserve 50% or more of a site for the future. Cost and law play roles but the **fundamental reason is scientific stewardship**.",
