        {
          "type": "concept",
          "title": "Potassium-Argon (K-Ar) and Argon-Argon Dating",
          "content": "When archaeologists work in **deep time** — millions of years for human ancestors — radiocarbon is useless. The method of choice becomes **potassium-argon (K-Ar)** dating.\n\n**The principle:**\n• Volcanic rocks contain **potassium-40 (K-40)**, which decays to **argon-40** with a half-life of **1.25 billion years**\n• When a volcano erupts, all argon escapes as gas\n• As the rock cools and crystallizes, argon-40 starts re-accumulating\n• Measure the K-40/Ar-40 ratio = time since cooling\n\n**Critical role in paleoanthropology:**\n• **Olduvai Gorge, Tanzania** — Mary and Louis Leakey's hominin discoveries dated by K-Ar of volcanic tuffs above and below the fossils. **Bracketing**: if the bone sits between a 1.85-million-year tuff and a 1.75-million-year tuff, the bone is in that window.\n• **Hadar, Ethiopia** — 'Lucy' (Australopithecus afarensis) dated to 3.2 million years using K-Ar of associated volcanic ash\n• **Laetoli footprints** dated to 3.6 million years by the same method\n\n**Argon-argon (Ar-Ar)** is a refined version requiring less rock and giving tighter precision. Both methods are essential to the **paleoanthropological time scale**.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "diagram",
            "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" class=\"lesson-visual\">\n                    <rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/>\n                    <text x=\"550\" y=\"70\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"36\">POTASSIUM-ARGON DATING</text>\n                    <text x=\"550\" y=\"115\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"24\">Reaching deep time</text>\n                    <rect x=\"100\" y=\"200\" width=\"900\" height=\"160\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(99,102,241,0.12)\" stroke=\"#6366f1\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n                    <text x=\"550\" y=\"255\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#6366f1\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"24\">THE PRINCIPLE</text>\n                    <text x=\"550\" y=\"300\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">K-40 → Ar-40, half-life 1.25 billion yrs</text>\n                    <text x=\"550\" y=\"335\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">Volcanic eruption resets the clock</text>\n                    <rect x=\"100\" y=\"380\" width=\"900\" height=\"160\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(139,92,246,0.12)\" stroke=\"#8b5cf6\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n                    <text x=\"550\" y=\"435\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#8b5cf6\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"24\">BRACKETING</text>\n                    <text x=\"550\" y=\"480\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">Date the volcanic ash above + below</text>\n                    <text x=\"550\" y=\"515\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"20\">Fossil age = sandwiched between</text>\n                    <rect x=\"80\" y=\"570\" width=\"940\" height=\"100\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(16,185,129,0.12)\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n                    <text x=\"120\" y=\"620\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"22\">OLDUVAI</text>\n                    <text x=\"420\" y=\"620\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"20\">Leakey hominins, 1.75-1.85 Ma</text>\n                    <rect x=\"80\" y=\"690\" width=\"940\" height=\"100\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(245,158,11,0.12)\" stroke=\"#f59e0b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n                    <text x=\"120\" y=\"740\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"22\">HADAR</text>\n                    <text x=\"420\" y=\"740\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"20\">Lucy, 3.2 million years</text>\n                    <rect x=\"80\" y=\"810\" width=\"940\" height=\"100\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(236,72,153,0.12)\" stroke=\"#ec4899\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n                    <text x=\"120\" y=\"860\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#ec4899\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"22\">LAETOLI</text>\n                    <text x=\"420\" y=\"860\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"20\">Footprints, 3.6 million years</text>\n                    <rect x=\"200\" y=\"940\" width=\"700\" height=\"60\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(255,215,0,0.1)\" stroke=\"#ffd700\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n                    <text x=\"550\" y=\"980\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-size=\"20\">Ar-Ar method is the modern refinement</text>\n                </svg>",
            "caption": "Dating human origins"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "concept",
          "title": "Thermoluminescence and Optically Stimulated Luminescence",
          "content": "What about pottery? Bricks? Burned flint? Radiocarbon can't date them — they're not organic. Enter **thermoluminescence (TL)** and its sibling **optically stimulated luminescence (OSL)**.\n\n**The principle:**\n• Crystalline materials (quartz, feldspar) trap electrons from background radiation over time\n• **Heating** above ~500°C (or strong light) **empties the traps**, resetting the clock to zero\n• Over the years, electrons accumulate again\n• In the lab, **heat** (TL) or **light** (OSL) the sample to release the electrons; the light emitted = age\n\n**TL is for heated objects:**\n• Fired pottery, baked clay figurines, burnt flint\n• Range: a few hundred to 500,000 years\n• Precision: ±5-10% (so a 4,000-year date might be ±200 years)\n\n**OSL is for buried sediments:**\n• Last time the sediment grain saw sunlight\n• Brilliant for dating **deposition events** — when did a dune form? When was a hearth buried?\n• Crucial for dating early **Homo sapiens** sites in places without organic preservation\n\nTL famously was used to expose forgeries: a 'medieval' brick that turns out to be 19th-century failed.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "diagram",
            "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" class=\"lesson-visual\">\n                    <rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/>\n                    <text x=\"550\" y=\"70\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"36\">LUMINESCENCE DATING</text>\n                    <text x=\"550\" y=\"115\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"24\">When carbon fails, light works</text>\n                    <rect x=\"100\" y=\"200\" width=\"900\" height=\"160\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(99,102,241,0.12)\" stroke=\"#6366f1\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n                    <text x=\"550\" y=\"255\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#6366f1\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"24\">THE TRAPPED ELECTRON</text>\n                    <text x=\"550\" y=\"300\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">Crystals trap radiation over time</text>\n                    <text x=\"550\" y=\"335\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">Heat or light releases them as glow</text>\n                    <rect x=\"80\" y=\"400\" width=\"440\" height=\"260\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(245,158,11,0.15)\" stroke=\"#f59e0b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n                    <text x=\"300\" y=\"455\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"24\">TL</text>\n                    <text x=\"300\" y=\"495\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"18\">Thermoluminescence</text>\n                    <text x=\"300\" y=\"545\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"20\">Heated objects</text>\n                    <text x=\"300\" y=\"585\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"20\">Pottery, burnt flint</text>\n                    <text x=\"300\" y=\"630\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"18\">±5-10% precision</text>\n                    <rect x=\"580\" y=\"400\" width=\"440\" height=\"260\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(16,185,129,0.15)\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n                    <text x=\"800\" y=\"455\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"24\">OSL</text>\n                    <text x=\"800\" y=\"495\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"18\">Optically Stimulated</text>\n                    <text x=\"800\" y=\"545\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"20\">Buried sediments</text>\n                    <text x=\"800\" y=\"585\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"20\">Dunes, hearths, sand</text>\n                    <text x=\"800\" y=\"630\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"18\">Last sunlight exposure</text>\n                    <rect x=\"100\" y=\"700\" width=\"900\" height=\"160\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(139,92,246,0.12)\" stroke=\"#8b5cf6\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n                    <text x=\"550\" y=\"755\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#8b5cf6\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"24\">RANGE</text>\n                    <text x=\"550\" y=\"800\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">A few hundred years to 500,000</text>\n                    <text x=\"550\" y=\"835\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"20\">Perfect when carbon won't reach</text>\n                    <rect x=\"200\" y=\"900\" width=\"700\" height=\"80\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(255,215,0,0.1)\" stroke=\"#ffd700\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n                    <text x=\"550\" y=\"950\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-size=\"22\">Also catches pottery forgers</text>\n                </svg>",
            "caption": "Light from trapped electrons"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "example",
          "title": "Multi-Method Dating at Ötzi the Iceman",
          "content": "When two German hikers found a body emerging from the Tisenjoch glacier in 1991, no one knew if it was a missing modern climber or something far older.\n\n**The full dating arsenal applied to Ötzi:**\n\n1. **Radiocarbon (C14)** on bone, hair, grass from his cloak: **3350-3105 BCE**, calibrated. Five separate AMS labs cross-checked. Result was extraordinarily consistent.\n\n2. **Dendrochronology** of his bow stave (yew): tree-ring patterns from the bow consistent with Late Neolithic Alpine yew populations.\n\n3. **Pollen analysis** of his stomach contents: pollen from local Alpine zones — hop hornbeam pollen indicated **spring/early summer** death.\n\n4. **Isotope analysis (Sr, O, Pb)** of his teeth and bones: showed he grew up in the Eisack Valley but died in the upper Etsch valley — **regional mobility** decoded.\n\n5. **Ancient DNA**: maternal haplogroup K, paternal G2a — placing him in Late Neolithic European populations.\n\nNo single method was sufficient. The **convergence of independent methods** is what made the result rock-solid. This is how modern archaeology works: **multiple lines of evidence**, all triangulating on the same answer.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "diagram",
            "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" class=\"lesson-visual\">\n                    <rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/>\n                    <text x=\"550\" y=\"70\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"36\">ÖTZI THE ICEMAN</text>\n                    <text x=\"550\" y=\"115\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"24\">Five methods, one date</text>\n                    <rect x=\"80\" y=\"200\" width=\"940\" height=\"100\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(99,102,241,0.12)\" stroke=\"#6366f1\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n                    <text x=\"120\" y=\"250\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#6366f1\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"20\">RADIOCARBON</text>\n                    <text x=\"450\" y=\"250\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"20\">5 labs: 3350-3105 BCE</text>\n                    <rect x=\"80\" y=\"320\" width=\"940\" height=\"100\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(139,92,246,0.12)\" stroke=\"#8b5cf6\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n                    <text x=\"120\" y=\"370\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#8b5cf6\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"20\">DENDRO BOW</text>\n                    <text x=\"450\" y=\"370\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"20\">Late Neolithic yew</text>\n                    <rect x=\"80\" y=\"440\" width=\"940\" height=\"100\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(16,185,129,0.12)\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n                    <text x=\"120\" y=\"490\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"20\">POLLEN</text>\n                    <text x=\"450\" y=\"490\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"20\">Death in spring/summer</text>\n                    <rect x=\"80\" y=\"560\" width=\"940\" height=\"100\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(245,158,11,0.12)\" stroke=\"#f59e0b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n                    <text x=\"120\" y=\"610\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"20\">ISOTOPES</text>\n                    <text x=\"450\" y=\"610\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"20\">Born Eisack, died Etsch</text>\n                    <rect x=\"80\" y=\"680\" width=\"940\" height=\"100\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(236,72,153,0.12)\" stroke=\"#ec4899\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n                    <text x=\"120\" y=\"730\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#ec4899\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"20\">ANCIENT DNA</text>\n                    <text x=\"450\" y=\"730\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"20\">Haplogroup K/G2a</text>\n                    <rect x=\"100\" y=\"800\" width=\"900\" height=\"200\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(255,215,0,0.1)\" stroke=\"#ffd700\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n                    <text x=\"550\" y=\"855\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"24\">CONVERGENCE</text>\n                    <text x=\"550\" y=\"900\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">All methods point to ~3300 BCE</text>\n                    <text x=\"550\" y=\"945\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">Late Neolithic, Alpine origin</text>\n                    <text x=\"550\" y=\"985\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"20\">Modern science demands triangulation</text>\n                </svg>",
            "caption": "Multiple methods, one answer"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "concept",
          "title": "Choosing the Right Method",
          "content": "There is no 'best' dating method. Each has a **time window, a material requirement, and a precision**. A good archaeologist matches method to question.\n\n**Quick reference:**\n• **Stratigraphy** — always, free, relative only\n• **Seriation** — large pottery samples, relative\n• **Dendrochronology** — wood with rings, exact year, ~13,000 years\n• **Radiocarbon** — organic, 50,000 yr limit, ±decades\n• **Thermoluminescence** — heated ceramic/flint, 500,000 yr limit, ±5-10%\n• **OSL** — buried sediment, 500,000 yr limit\n• **Uranium-series** — bone/coral/cave deposits, 500,000 yr limit\n• **Potassium-Argon** — volcanic rock, deep time\n• **Electron Spin Resonance (ESR)** — tooth enamel, 2 million yr limit\n• **Cosmogenic nuclides** — exposed rock surfaces, glaciation timing\n\n**The professional rule**: never trust a single method. Sites get dated by **multiple independent techniques** wherever possible. Discrepancies trigger re-examination of stratigraphy, sample contamination, or calibration.\n\nThe best archaeological dating sits at the **intersection of methods that should not lie together**.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "diagram",
            "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" class=\"lesson-visual\">\n                    <rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/>\n                    <text x=\"550\" y=\"70\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"36\">DATING DECISION TREE</text>\n                    <text x=\"550\" y=\"115\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"24\">Match method to material</text>\n                    <rect x=\"80\" y=\"200\" width=\"940\" height=\"100\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(99,102,241,0.12)\" stroke=\"#6366f1\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n                    <text x=\"120\" y=\"245\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#6366f1\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"20\">WOOD?</text>\n                    <text x=\"450\" y=\"245\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"20\">Dendrochronology + C14</text>\n                    <text x=\"450\" y=\"280\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"16\">Year precision possible</text>\n                    <rect x=\"80\" y=\"320\" width=\"940\" height=\"100\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(139,92,246,0.12)\" stroke=\"#8b5cf6\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n                    <text x=\"120\" y=\"365\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#8b5cf6\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"20\">BONE/CHARCOAL?</text>\n                    <text x=\"450\" y=\"365\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"20\">Radiocarbon (AMS)</text>\n                    <text x=\"450\" y=\"400\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"16\">If under 50,000 years old</text>\n                    <rect x=\"80\" y=\"440\" width=\"940\" height=\"100\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(16,185,129,0.12)\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n                    <text x=\"120\" y=\"485\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"20\">POTTERY/BRICK?</text>\n                    <text x=\"450\" y=\"485\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"20\">Thermoluminescence</text>\n                    <text x=\"450\" y=\"520\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"16\">If kiln-fired above 500C</text>\n                    <rect x=\"80\" y=\"560\" width=\"940\" height=\"100\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(245,158,11,0.12)\" stroke=\"#f59e0b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n                    <text x=\"120\" y=\"605\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"20\">BURIED SAND?</text>\n                    <text x=\"450\" y=\"605\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"20\">OSL</text>\n                    <text x=\"450\" y=\"640\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"16\">Dates last sunlight exposure</text>\n                    <rect x=\"80\" y=\"680\" width=\"940\" height=\"100\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(236,72,153,0.12)\" stroke=\"#ec4899\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n                    <text x=\"120\" y=\"725\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#ec4899\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"20\">VOLCANIC ASH?</text>\n                    <text x=\"450\" y=\"725\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"20\">K-Ar or Ar-Ar</text>\n                    <text x=\"450\" y=\"760\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"16\">For hominin-era dating</text>\n                    <rect x=\"80\" y=\"800\" width=\"940\" height=\"100\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(59,130,246,0.12)\" stroke=\"#6366f1\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n                    <text x=\"120\" y=\"845\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#6366f1\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"20\">TOOTH ENAMEL?</text>\n                    <text x=\"450\" y=\"845\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"20\">ESR or U-series</text>\n                    <text x=\"450\" y=\"880\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"16\">Reaches 2 million years</text>\n                    <rect x=\"100\" y=\"920\" width=\"900\" height=\"80\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(255,215,0,0.1)\" stroke=\"#ffd700\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n                    <text x=\"550\" y=\"970\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-size=\"22\">Always use multiple methods</text>\n                </svg>",
            "caption": "Picking a dating method"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "example",
          "title": "When Dating Saves a Theory — and Kills One",
          "content": "**The Tutankhamun mask date (saved):** When KV62 was opened in 1922, skeptics whispered Howard Carter had salted the tomb with later objects. Radiocarbon dates on textiles from the burial put everything firmly in the Late Bronze Age, ~1325 BCE. Theory: confirmed.\n\n**The Piltdown Man hoax (killed):** Discovered 1912, 'Piltdown Man' was hailed as the 'missing link.' For four decades, British scientists defended it. In 1953, **fluorine dating** of the bone and **thermoluminescence-style chemical testing** revealed the jaw was a modern orangutan, the cranium medieval human, both stained to look ancient. **Dating exposed one of science's greatest frauds.**\n\n**Cave art at Chauvet (revolutionized):** Conservative dating put cave painting at ~15,000 BP. Then radiocarbon on the **pigment itself** (not the wall) pushed Chauvet to **32,000-30,000 BP** — doubling the age of cave art and overturning assumptions about cognitive evolution.\n\n**Australian arrival (still moving):** OSL dating at Madjedbebe in 2017 pushed human arrival in Australia to **65,000 BP**, ~15,000 years earlier than the previous consensus.\n\nDating doesn't just confirm history. It **rewrites** it.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "diagram",
            "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" class=\"lesson-visual\">\n                    <rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/>\n                    <text x=\"550\" y=\"70\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"36\">WHEN DATING CHANGES EVERYTHING</text>\n                    <text x=\"550\" y=\"115\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"24\">Four landmark cases</text>\n                    <rect x=\"100\" y=\"200\" width=\"900\" height=\"160\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(16,185,129,0.12)\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n                    <text x=\"550\" y=\"255\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"22\">TUTANKHAMUN (SAVED)</text>\n                    <text x=\"550\" y=\"300\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"20\">C14 textiles confirmed 1325 BCE</text>\n                    <text x=\"550\" y=\"335\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"18\">Refuted hoax accusations</text>\n                    <rect x=\"100\" y=\"380\" width=\"900\" height=\"160\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(239,68,68,0.1)\" stroke=\"#ef4444\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n                    <text x=\"550\" y=\"435\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ef4444\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"22\">PILTDOWN (KILLED)</text>\n                    <text x=\"550\" y=\"480\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"20\">Fluorine + chemistry exposed fraud</text>\n                    <text x=\"550\" y=\"515\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"18\">1953 - decades of belief overturned</text>\n                    <rect x=\"100\" y=\"560\" width=\"900\" height=\"160\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(139,92,246,0.12)\" stroke=\"#8b5cf6\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n                    <text x=\"550\" y=\"615\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#8b5cf6\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"22\">CHAUVET (REVOLUTIONIZED)</text>\n                    <text x=\"550\" y=\"660\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"20\">C14 pigment: 32,000 BP</text>\n                    <text x=\"550\" y=\"695\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"18\">Doubled the age of cave art</text>\n                    <rect x=\"100\" y=\"740\" width=\"900\" height=\"160\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(245,158,11,0.12)\" stroke=\"#f59e0b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n                    <text x=\"550\" y=\"795\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"22\">AUSTRALIA (MOVED)</text>\n                    <text x=\"550\" y=\"840\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"20\">OSL Madjedbebe: 65,000 BP</text>\n                    <text x=\"550\" y=\"875\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"18\">15,000 years earlier than thought</text>\n                    <rect x=\"200\" y=\"930\" width=\"700\" height=\"60\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(255,215,0,0.1)\" stroke=\"#ffd700\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n                    <text x=\"550\" y=\"970\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-size=\"22\">Dating IS the science</text>\n                </svg>",
            "caption": "Dates that changed history"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "quiz",
          "question": "You're dating a 2.5-million-year-old hominin tooth found near a volcanic ash layer. Which technique should you use?",
          "options": [
            {
              "text": "Radiocarbon dating on the tooth enamel",
              "correct": false
            },
            {
              "text": "Dendrochronology on the nearest preserved wood",
              "correct": false
            },
            {
              "text": "Potassium-argon (or Ar-Ar) dating on the volcanic ash, bracketing the tooth",
              "correct": true
            },
            {
              "text": "Optically Stimulated Luminescence on the surrounding sediment",
              "correct": false
            }
          ],
          "explanation": "**Radiocarbon's maximum range is ~50,000 years** — useless at 2.5 million. **OSL maxes out around 500,000 years**. **Dendrochronology** only reaches ~13,000 years and would require wood, which rarely survives that long. **Potassium-argon (K-Ar) or argon-argon (Ar-Ar)** dating of volcanic rock has a range stretching into billions of years and is the standard tool for hominin sites in East Africa. The technique 'brackets' the fossil between two dated ash layers.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "diagram",
            "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" class=\"lesson-visual\">\n                    <rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/>\n                    <text x=\"550\" y=\"70\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"36\">KNOWLEDGE CHECK</text>\n                    <text x=\"550\" y=\"115\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"24\">Picking the right tool</text>\n                    <rect x=\"150\" y=\"220\" width=\"800\" height=\"120\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(239,68,68,0.1)\" stroke=\"#ef4444\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n                    <text x=\"550\" y=\"275\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ef4444\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"22\">2.5 MILLION YEARS</text>\n                    <text x=\"550\" y=\"315\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"20\">Way past C14, OSL, dendro</text>\n                    <rect x=\"150\" y=\"380\" width=\"800\" height=\"220\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(16,185,129,0.1)\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n                    <text x=\"550\" y=\"445\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"24\">POTASSIUM-ARGON</text>\n                    <text x=\"550\" y=\"500\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">Date the volcanic ash above + below</text>\n                    <text x=\"550\" y=\"540\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">Sandwiched fossil = age between</text>\n                    <text x=\"550\" y=\"580\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"20\">Half-life 1.25 billion years</text>\n                </svg>",
            "caption": "Deep time tool"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "practice",
          "title": "Practice: Pick the Right Method",
          "content": "**Exercise.** For each material below, name the BEST primary dating method, give your reasoning, and note one limitation.\n\nA. A waterlogged Neolithic oak post from a Swiss lake-village (well-preserved, ~5000 years old)\n\nB. A burnt clay figurine from a Greek Bronze Age house, kiln-fired then buried under collapsed mud-brick\n\nC. A 1.8-million-year-old hominin tooth from an East African rift-valley site, surrounded by volcanic tuff layers\n\nD. A sand dune in Australia that buried a Pleistocene stone tool assemblage\n\nE. A charred grain found in a Roman granary\n\n**Model answer.**\n\nA. **Dendrochronology + AMS radiocarbon** — wet wood preserves rings; tree-ring date can hit a single year. Limitation: needs a regional master chronology.\n\nB. **Thermoluminescence (TL)** — clay heated above 500°C resets the trap clock. Limitation: ±5-10% precision, ~±200-400 years for a Bronze Age date.\n\nC. **Potassium-Argon (K-Ar) or Ar-Ar** on the volcanic tuffs above/below the tooth — bracketing technique. Limitation: needs unweathered volcanic crystals; uncertainty grows for younger tuffs.\n\nD. **OSL** — dates the last time the quartz grains saw sunlight before burial. Limitation: assumes the grains were fully bleached at deposition.\n\nE. **AMS radiocarbon** on the grain itself. Limitation: must avoid 'old wood' contamination; charred seeds are short-lived so best for tight dating.\n\nThe principle: **match the clock to the material, and know what each method assumes**.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "diagram",
            "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" class=\"lesson-visual\">\n                    <rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/>\n                    <text x=\"550\" y=\"70\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"36\">PRACTICE</text>\n                    <text x=\"550\" y=\"115\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"24\">Pick the right clock</text>\n                    <rect x=\"80\" y=\"200\" width=\"940\" height=\"100\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(99,102,241,0.12)\" stroke=\"#6366f1\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n                    <text x=\"120\" y=\"245\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#6366f1\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"20\">A. OAK POST</text>\n                    <text x=\"450\" y=\"245\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"20\">Dendro + AMS</text>\n                    <text x=\"450\" y=\"280\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"16\">Year precision</text>\n                    <rect x=\"80\" y=\"320\" width=\"940\" height=\"100\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(139,92,246,0.12)\" stroke=\"#8b5cf6\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n                    <text x=\"120\" y=\"365\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#8b5cf6\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"20\">B. FIGURINE</text>\n                    <text x=\"450\" y=\"365\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"20\">TL on heated clay</text>\n                    <text x=\"450\" y=\"400\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"16\">±5-10%</text>\n                    <rect x=\"80\" y=\"440\" width=\"940\" height=\"100\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(16,185,129,0.12)\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n                    <text x=\"120\" y=\"485\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"20\">C. TOOTH</text>\n                    <text x=\"450\" y=\"485\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"20\">K-Ar on ash brackets</text>\n                    <text x=\"450\" y=\"520\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"16\">Sandwich the fossil</text>\n                    <rect x=\"80\" y=\"560\" width=\"940\" height=\"100\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(245,158,11,0.12)\" stroke=\"#f59e0b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n                    <text x=\"120\" y=\"605\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"20\">D. DUNE</text>\n                    <text x=\"450\" y=\"605\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"20\">OSL on sand grains</text>\n                    <text x=\"450\" y=\"640\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"16\">Last sunlight</text>\n                    <rect x=\"80\" y=\"680\" width=\"940\" height=\"100\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(236,72,153,0.12)\" stroke=\"#ec4899\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n                    <text x=\"120\" y=\"725\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#ec4899\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"20\">E. GRAIN</text>\n                    <text x=\"450\" y=\"725\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"20\">AMS C14 on charred seed</text>\n                    <text x=\"450\" y=\"760\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"16\">Short-lived ideal</text>\n                    <rect x=\"200\" y=\"810\" width=\"700\" height=\"160\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(255,215,0,0.1)\" stroke=\"#ffd700\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n                    <text x=\"550\" y=\"870\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-size=\"22\">Match the clock to the material</text>\n                    <text x=\"550\" y=\"915\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"20\">and respect each method's assumptions</text>\n                </svg>",
            "caption": "Method matching exercise"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "practice",
          "title": "Practice: Diagnose a Date Disagreement",
          "content": "**Exercise.** Two AMS radiocarbon dates are returned from a single Neolithic burial:\n\n• Date 1: charcoal from grave fill = **5800 ± 30 BP** → calibrated 4720-4555 cal BCE\n• Date 2: human bone collagen from the skeleton = **5500 ± 30 BP** → calibrated 4445-4255 cal BCE\n\nA 300-year radiocarbon-year gap. Which date do you trust, and why? What might explain the discrepancy?\n\n**Model answer.**\n\n**The bone is more reliable for dating the burial event** because it is **directly tied to the person**. The charcoal could come from any wood that ended up in the fill — including reused old timbers ('old wood effect'), or it could be intrusive material that washed in later.\n\n**Possible explanations:**\n1. **Old wood effect** — the charcoal came from the outer rings of a long-lived tree; the death of the tree predates the burial by centuries\n2. **Residual material** — the charcoal was already in the soil when the grave was dug\n3. **Marine reservoir effect** — if the person ate mostly marine protein, the bone collagen would be 'too old' by ~400 years (not 'too young' here, so less likely)\n4. **Sample contamination** — modern carbon contamination would make the bone look younger\n\n**Best practice:**\n• Use SHORT-LIVED material when possible (charred seeds, twigs, single-year bone)\n• Date directly on the EVENT (the body, not the fill)\n• Run multiple samples and use BAYESIAN MODELING (OxCal) to integrate stratigraphic constraints\n\nThe principle: **a single date is a hint; multiple dates plus stratigraphic logic give you a fact**.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "diagram",
            "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" class=\"lesson-visual\">\n                    <rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/>\n                    <text x=\"550\" y=\"70\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"36\">PRACTICE</text>\n                    <text x=\"550\" y=\"115\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"24\">Diagnose date disagreement</text>\n                    <rect x=\"80\" y=\"200\" width=\"440\" height=\"200\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(239,68,68,0.1)\" stroke=\"#ef4444\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n                    <text x=\"300\" y=\"260\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ef4444\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"22\">CHARCOAL</text>\n                    <text x=\"300\" y=\"310\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"20\">5800 BP</text>\n                    <text x=\"300\" y=\"355\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"18\">Suspect: old wood</text>\n                    <rect x=\"580\" y=\"200\" width=\"440\" height=\"200\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(16,185,129,0.12)\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n                    <text x=\"800\" y=\"260\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"22\">BONE</text>\n                    <text x=\"800\" y=\"310\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"20\">5500 BP</text>\n                    <text x=\"800\" y=\"355\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"18\">Trust: tied to event</text>\n                    <rect x=\"100\" y=\"450\" width=\"900\" height=\"160\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(245,158,11,0.12)\" stroke=\"#f59e0b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n                    <text x=\"550\" y=\"505\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"24\">LIKELY CAUSE</text>\n                    <text x=\"550\" y=\"555\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">Old wood effect on charcoal</text>\n                    <text x=\"550\" y=\"590\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"20\">Outer rings of long-lived tree</text>\n                    <rect x=\"100\" y=\"640\" width=\"900\" height=\"160\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(139,92,246,0.12)\" stroke=\"#8b5cf6\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n                    <text x=\"550\" y=\"695\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#8b5cf6\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"24\">FIX</text>\n                    <text x=\"550\" y=\"745\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">Short-lived samples + Bayesian model</text>\n                    <text x=\"550\" y=\"780\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"20\">Multiple direct-on-event dates</text>\n                    <rect x=\"150\" y=\"830\" width=\"800\" height=\"140\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(255,215,0,0.1)\" stroke=\"#ffd700\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n                    <text x=\"550\" y=\"885\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-size=\"22\">One date = hint. Many dates = fact.</text>\n                    <text x=\"550\" y=\"935\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"20\">Read stratigraphy alongside numbers</text>\n                </svg>",
            "caption": "Date disagreement diagnosis"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "application",
          "title": "Reading a Real Site Report's Dates",
          "content": "Next time you read an archaeological paper, look at how they report dates. Apply this checklist:\n\n1. **Multiple methods?** A single radiocarbon date is suspicious. Look for 3+ independent dates from different materials.\n\n2. **Calibrated?** 'BP' alone is uncalibrated. Look for 'cal BCE/CE' or '2σ' (95% probability) ranges.\n\n3. **Lab code reported?** Quality reports list the lab code (e.g., OxA-12345) so others can verify.\n\n4. **Material specified?** What was dated — bone collagen, charred seed, wood charcoal? Each has its own pitfalls.\n\n5. **Context recorded?** A date is only useful if the sample's stratigraphic position is known. 'C14 date from somewhere in the site' = worthless.\n\n6. **Cross-check with stratigraphy?** Do the dates respect superposition? If not, the authors should explain the inversion.\n\n7. **Bayesian modeling used?** Modern best practice: combine all dates with stratigraphic constraints into a Bayesian model (OxCal software). This tightens ranges dramatically.\n\nKnow these and you can spot weak archaeology in 30 seconds.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "diagram",
            "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" class=\"lesson-visual\">\n                    <rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/>\n                    <text x=\"550\" y=\"70\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"36\">DATE-READER'S CHECKLIST</text>\n                    <text x=\"550\" y=\"115\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"24\">Spotting weak dating</text>\n                    <rect x=\"150\" y=\"190\" width=\"800\" height=\"90\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(99,102,241,0.12)\" stroke=\"#6366f1\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n                    <text x=\"200\" y=\"245\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#6366f1\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"22\">1.</text>\n                    <text x=\"250\" y=\"245\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"20\">Multiple independent methods?</text>\n                    <rect x=\"150\" y=\"300\" width=\"800\" height=\"90\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(139,92,246,0.12)\" stroke=\"#8b5cf6\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n                    <text x=\"200\" y=\"355\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#8b5cf6\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"22\">2.</text>\n                    <text x=\"250\" y=\"355\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"20\">Calibrated to cal BCE?</text>\n                    <rect x=\"150\" y=\"410\" width=\"800\" height=\"90\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(16,185,129,0.12)\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n                    <text x=\"200\" y=\"465\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"22\">3.</text>\n                    <text x=\"250\" y=\"465\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"20\">Lab code reported?</text>\n                    <rect x=\"150\" y=\"520\" width=\"800\" height=\"90\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(245,158,11,0.12)\" stroke=\"#f59e0b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n                    <text x=\"200\" y=\"575\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"22\">4.</text>\n                    <text x=\"250\" y=\"575\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"20\">Material specified?</text>\n                    <rect x=\"150\" y=\"630\" width=\"800\" height=\"90\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(236,72,153,0.12)\" stroke=\"#ec4899\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n                    <text x=\"200\" y=\"685\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#ec4899\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"22\">5.</text>\n                    <text x=\"250\" y=\"685\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"20\">Stratigraphic context recorded?</text>\n                    <rect x=\"150\" y=\"740\" width=\"800\" height=\"90\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(20,184,166,0.15)\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n                    <text x=\"200\" y=\"795\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"22\">6.</text>\n                    <text x=\"250\" y=\"795\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"20\">Dates respect superposition?</text>\n                    <rect x=\"150\" y=\"850\" width=\"800\" height=\"90\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(59,130,246,0.12)\" stroke=\"#6366f1\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n                    <text x=\"200\" y=\"905\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#6366f1\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"22\">7.</text>\n                    <text x=\"250\" y=\"905\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"20\">Bayesian model (OxCal)?</text>\n                </svg>",
            "caption": "Critical reading habits"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "concept",
          "title": "Insider Knowledge: Older Than Stonehenge",
          "body": "Stonehenge feels impossibly ancient — yet Göbekli Tepe in Turkey predates it by roughly 6,000 years. Built ~11,500 years ago by HUNTER-GATHERERS, before pottery, writing, the wheel, or even agriculture, its massive carved stone pillars upend the old story that civilization required farming first. The shock is the order of events: people may have built monumental temples and THEN settled down to farm, not the reverse. It quietly rewrote the timeline of civilization itself.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "diagram",
            "caption": "Gobekli Tepe predates Stonehenge and the pyramids by millennia.",
            "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><rect width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"70\" font-size=\"36\" fill=\"#ffd700\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"Arial\" font-weight=\"bold\">Rewriting the Timeline</text><line x1=\"120\" y1=\"900\" x2=\"980\" y2=\"900\" stroke=\"#ffffff\" stroke-width=\"4\"/><circle cx=\"180\" cy=\"900\" r=\"14\" fill=\"#e94560\"/><text x=\"180\" y=\"860\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#ffd700\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"Arial\">~9500 BCE</text><text x=\"180\" y=\"960\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"Arial\">Gobekli Tepe</text><circle cx=\"620\" cy=\"900\" r=\"14\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/><text x=\"620\" y=\"860\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#ffd700\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"Arial\">~3000 BCE</text><text x=\"620\" y=\"960\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"Arial\">Stonehenge</text><circle cx=\"800\" cy=\"900\" r=\"14\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/><text x=\"800\" y=\"860\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#ffd700\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"Arial\">~2560 BCE</text><text x=\"800\" y=\"960\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"Arial\">Great Pyramid</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"500\" font-size=\"26\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"Arial\">Built by hunter-gatherers</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"550\" font-size=\"26\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"Arial\">BEFORE agriculture</text></svg>"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "quiz",
          "question": "Why is dendrochronology often used to CALIBRATE radiocarbon dating, rather than the other way around?",
          "options": [
            {
              "text": "Dendrochronology can date materials older than radiocarbon can reach",
              "correct": false
            },
            {
              "text": "Tree rings provide an independent calendar-year anchor that radiocarbon cannot produce on its own",
              "correct": true
            },
            {
              "text": "Radiocarbon is too expensive for most labs",
              "correct": false
            },
            {
              "text": "Tree rings work on a wider range of materials than radiocarbon",
              "correct": false
            }
          ],
          "explanation": "Dendrochronology gives you the **exact calendar year** a tree ring formed — a true atomic-clock-style anchor. Radiocarbon ages, by contrast, drift because atmospheric C14 varied historically. By radiocarbon-dating wood samples whose calendar age is already known from tree rings, scientists build the **IntCal calibration curve**: a master conversion table from raw 'BP' to true calendar years. Without dendrochronology, radiocarbon would be much less accurate.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "diagram",
            "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" class=\"lesson-visual\">\n                    <rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/>\n                    <text x=\"550\" y=\"70\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"36\">FINAL CHECK</text>\n                    <text x=\"550\" y=\"115\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"24\">The calibration partnership</text>\n                    <rect x=\"80\" y=\"220\" width=\"440\" height=\"280\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(245,158,11,0.12)\" stroke=\"#f59e0b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n                    <text x=\"300\" y=\"285\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"24\">DENDROCHRONOLOGY</text>\n                    <text x=\"300\" y=\"340\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">True calendar year</text>\n                    <text x=\"300\" y=\"395\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">Exact, anchored</text>\n                    <text x=\"300\" y=\"450\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"20\">The standard</text>\n                    <rect x=\"580\" y=\"220\" width=\"440\" height=\"280\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(139,92,246,0.12)\" stroke=\"#8b5cf6\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n                    <text x=\"800\" y=\"285\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#8b5cf6\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"24\">RADIOCARBON</text>\n                    <text x=\"800\" y=\"340\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">Raw 'BP' years</text>\n                    <text x=\"800\" y=\"395\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">Drifts with atmosphere</text>\n                    <text x=\"800\" y=\"450\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"20\">Needs calibration</text>\n                    <rect x=\"150\" y=\"560\" width=\"800\" height=\"280\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(255,215,0,0.1)\" stroke=\"#ffd700\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n                    <text x=\"550\" y=\"630\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"24\">INTCAL CURVE</text>\n                    <text x=\"550\" y=\"690\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">Tree rings calibrate carbon</text>\n                    <text x=\"550\" y=\"745\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">Master conversion table</text>\n                    <text x=\"550\" y=\"800\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"20\">BP raw → cal BCE calendar</text>\n                </svg>",
            "caption": "How calibration works"
          }
        }
