          "explanation": "**Stonehenge dates to 3000-2200 BCE**. **Druids first appear around 250 BCE**, attested by Caesar, Pliny, and Tacitus during the Iron Age and Roman conquest of Britain. By that point Stonehenge had been abandoned as a working sacred site for **over a thousand years** — comparable to modern people claiming to have built the Pyramids. The Druid-Stonehenge link was an antiquarian fantasy popularized by **William Stukeley in 1740** and has stuck in popular culture ever since.",
