          "explanation": "Egyptian archaeology has adopted the same **conservation ethic** that governs modern archaeology globally: **sites are irreplaceable, and excavation is destructive**. Non-invasive methods like **muon tomography** (Great Pyramid void), **GPR surveys** (KV62 walls), **Djedi robotics** (Khufu air shafts), and **multispectral imaging** allow researchers to extract huge amounts of information without disturbing context. Future technologies will see even more — but only if we leave material undisturbed. Egyptian authorities still permit major excavations; the choice to use non-invasive methods is scientific, not political.",
