          "explanation": "The **PACUNAM LiDAR Initiative (2018)** mapped 2,144 sq km of Guatemalan jungle and identified **60,000+ previously unknown structures** — house mounds, terraces, roads, fortifications. This data **revised Classic Maya central lowland population estimates from ~5 million to 10-15 million**, making the Maya world demographically comparable to medieval Europe. The change has been seismic in Mesoamerican archaeology and confirms that **the Maya were a hyperdense agricultural civilization**, not a scattering of ceremonial centers. Earlier estimates were unreliable simply because the canopy hid the data.",
