          "explanation": "The **Uluburun wreck's cargo** was an unprecedented Bronze Age trade snapshot: **Cypriot copper, central Asian tin, sub-Saharan ebony, hippo ivory, Egyptian scarabs (one with Nefertiti's name), Levantine amphorae, Mycenaean seals, Baltic amber, and more**. Before Uluburun, the scale of Bronze Age trade was debated; now it's confirmed that the **Mediterranean operated as a single interconnected system** with luxury and bulk goods circulating freely. No crown of Tutankhamun, log book, or printed books were aboard — the value is in the diversity of bulk cargo proving the scope of long-distance trade.",
