          "type": "concept",
          "title": "Insider Knowledge: A King Under a Car Park",
          "body": "In 2012, archaeologists found the long-lost remains of King Richard III of England — not in a cathedral, but beneath a council PARKING LOT in Leicester. Records said he was buried at a friary later demolished; researchers traced its footprint to the asphalt above. A skeleton with battle wounds and a curved spine matched the historical king, and DNA from living relatives confirmed it. A monarch dead for 500 years was identified by genetics under a painted parking space marked 'R'.",
