          "explanation": "Because **diving time is severely limited** (bottom time, decompression schedules, depth limits), underwater archaeologists have **mastered non-invasive remote-sensing technology** earlier and more thoroughly than many terrestrial colleagues. **Side-scan sonar, ROVs, AUVs, 3D photogrammetry, AI image analysis, sediment DNA, and digital twin construction** are all standard before any artifact is touched. The Black Sea MAP excavated 65+ wrecks WITHOUT physical excavation — pure documentation. Land archaeology is now learning from underwater archaeology about prioritizing non-invasive documentation, especially for fragile sites.",
